# Kernel report

What `largo prove --kernel <document> --json` prints, read. (`largo check
--kernel --json` prints the same bytes; both were recorded for every document in
`tests/fixtures/kernel/`.) The report is one JSON object with sorted keys:
`blocks` (each `block` number and its `output`), `checked`, `error`,
`failed_block` (`null` when the document did not even parse), `file` and
`surface`, which is always `kernel_document`.

## Note
A report, read: whether the document checked, each block's output in order, the
first refused block (`0` when none is named) and the kernel's error.

## A KernelReport has:
    a checked, which is Bool.
    an outputs, which is Seq of Text.
    a failedBlock, which is Int.
    an error, which is Text.

## Note
The report in `stdout`, or why it is not one: the blocks must be numbered 1, 2, 3, …
in order with a text output each, and the surface must be the kernel's.

## To parseKernelReport (stdout: Text) -> Result of KernelReport and Text:
    Inspect jsonTryParse(trim(stdout)):
        When JErr (m):
            Return a new Err with error "the report is not JSON: " + m.
        When JOk (v):
            Let surface be jsonSerialize(jsonGet(v, "surface")).
            If surface is not equal to "\"kernel_document\"":
                Return a new Err with error "the report is not a kernel document report".
            Let checked be jsonSerialize(jsonGet(v, "checked")) is equal to "true".
            Let mutable report be a new KernelReport with checked checked and outputs [] and failedBlock 0 and error "".
            Inspect jsonGet(v, "failed_block"):
                When JNum (k):
                    Set report's failedBlock to k.
                Otherwise:
                    Set report's failedBlock to 0.
            Inspect jsonGet(v, "error"):
                When JStr (m):
                    Set report's error to m.
                Otherwise:
                    Set report's error to "".
            Inspect jsonGet(v, "blocks"):
                When JArr (blocks):
                    Repeat for b in blocks:
                        Let numbered be jsonSerialize(jsonGet(b, "block")).
                        If numbered is not equal to "{length of report's outputs + 1}":
                            Return a new Err with error "the report numbers its blocks out of order".
                        Inspect jsonGet(b, "output"):
                            When JStr (out):
                                Set report's outputs to report's outputs + [out].
                            Otherwise:
                                Return a new Err with error "a block of the report has no output".
                Otherwise:
                    Return a new Err with error "the report has no block list".
            Return a new Ok with value report.
    Return a new Err with error "unreadable report".

## Note
The axioms a `Print Axioms <name>.` output names: the kernel prints
`'n' depends on no axioms` or `'n' depends on axioms: [a, b]`.

## To axiomsOf (output: Text, name: Text) -> Result of Seq of Text and Text:
    If output is equal to "'" + name + "' depends on no axioms":
        Return a new Ok with value [].
    Let lead be "'" + name + "' depends on axioms: [".
    If startsWith(output, lead) is equal to false or endsWith(output, "]") is equal to false:
        Return a new Err with error "`{output}` is not the axiom report of {name}".
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for part in split(removeSuffix(removePrefix(output, lead), "]"), ","):
        If trim(part) is not equal to "":
            Push trim(part) to out.
    Return a new Ok with value out.

## Note
What a name probe found: `bound` when the probe checked, `free` when the kernel
answered that the name is unbound, `unknown` for anything else.

## To probeOutcome (exitCode: Int, stdout: Text, name: Text) -> Text:
    Inspect parseKernelReport(stdout):
        When Ok (r):
            If r's checked and exitCode is equal to 0:
                Return "bound".
            If r's checked is equal to false and r's error is equal to "Kernel error: Unbound variable: " + name:
                Return "free".
            Return "unknown".
        When Err (e):
            Return "unknown".
    Return "unknown".

## Test: a checked report reads block by block

Let text be "{{\"blocks\":[{{\"block\":1,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":2,\"output\":\"proof_of_goal : goal\"}}],\"checked\":true,\"error\":null,\"failed_block\":null,\"file\":\"f\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
Expect that parseKernelReport(text) is equal to a new Ok with value (a new KernelReport with checked true and outputs ["", "proof_of_goal : goal"] and failedBlock 0 and error "").
Expect that parseKernelReport("[1]") is equal to a new Err with error "the report is not a kernel document report".

## Test: the axiom report reads both of its forms

Expect that axiomsOf("'p' depends on no axioms", "p") is equal to a new Ok with value [].
Expect that axiomsOf("'p' depends on axioms: [Classical_choice, Quot_sound, propext]", "p") is equal to a new Ok with value ["Classical_choice", "Quot_sound", "propext"].
Expect that axiomsOf("'q' depends on no axioms", "p") is equal to a new Err with error "`'q' depends on no axioms` is not the axiom report of p".

## Test: a probe is bound only when it checked, free only when unbound by name

For all booleans checked:
    Let mutable text be "{{\"blocks\":[],\"checked\":false,\"error\":\"Kernel error: Unbound variable: x\",\"failed_block\":1,\"file\":\"f\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
    Let mutable code be 1.
    Let mutable expected be "free".
    If checked:
        Set text to "{{\"blocks\":[{{\"block\":1,\"output\":\"x : Nat\"}}],\"checked\":true,\"error\":null,\"failed_block\":null,\"file\":\"f\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
        Set code to 0.
        Set expected to "bound".
    Expect that probeOutcome(code, text, "x") is equal to expected.
    Expect that probeOutcome(code, text, "y") is equal to "unknown" or checked.
